  "_design": {
    "notes": "30 fps forward-then-reverse scrub over every frame in an 80-frame series. Demand is 30 frames/s; at 32 KB that is ~7.9 Mbps and at 250 KB ~62 Mbps, so the cells actually bind. Every want is a first visit on the forward pass, so p95 measures real transport wait rather than cache hits."
